✔ the overlap predicate counts only writes whose whole interval is strictly inside the copy (2.8162ms)
﹣ a backup of a database of 300 MB or more completes within the bound while another process commits writes inside the copy, and passes an integrity check (4.3412ms) # resource-intensive: set STYLE_LARGE_BACKUP_TEST=1 to run
✔ a completed backup is sanitised, verified and published under a final name only (6847.7414ms)
✔ a failure at any stage leaves no final file, no partial and no marker bytes, and keeps the earlier backup and the live data (4005.7482ms)
✔ pruning happens only after a backup completed (1930.4831ms)
✔ a cleanup that cannot remove the partial says so instead of claiming it is gone (1512.2269ms)
✔ a killed owner leaves only a partial that restore refuses; its lock dies with it, the next backup takes over at once and removes the dead partial (17239.2746ms)
✔ two contenders waiting on a live owner cannot take its lock; when it is killed they proceed one at a time and both succeed (17787.8392ms)
